{"id":"mahabharata-12-161","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":161,"title":"एकषष्ट्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 161 · Dharma, wealth and desire again","summary":{"en":"After Bhishma stops, Yudhishthira asks which is the greater of dharma, wealth and desire, and Bhishma says that they are interdependent, but liberation is above all. He tells of how those who want wealth, others who want heaven and a few who want liberation each follow their way.","kn":"ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಮೌನವಾದ ನಂತರ ಧರ್ಮ, ಅರ್ಥ, ಕಾಮದಲ್ಲಿ ಯಾವುದು ಹೆಚ್ಚೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವು ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಅವಲಂಬಿತ, ಆದರೆ ಮೋಕ್ಷ ಎಲ್ಲಕ್ಕಿಂತ ಮೇಲೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧನ ಬಯಸುವವರು, ಸ್ವರ್ಗ ಬಯಸುವವರು, ಮೋಕ್ಷ ಬಯಸುವ ಕೆಲವರು ತಮ್ಮ ತಮ್ಮ ಮಾರ್ಗ ಅನುಸರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"भीष्म के रुकने पर युधिष्ठिर पूछते हैं कि धर्म, अर्थ और काम में कौन बड़ा है, और भीष्म कहते हैं कि वे परस्पर निर्भर हैं पर मोक्ष सबसे ऊपर है। वे बताते हैं कि धन, स्वर्ग या मोक्ष चाहने वाले अपना-अपना मार्ग चलते हैं।","te":"భీష్ముడు ఆగాక ధర్మ, అర్థ, కామాల్లో ఏది గొప్పదని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు; అవి పరస్పర ఆధారాలని, కానీ మోక్షం అన్నిటికంటే పైనని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు. ధనం కోరేవారు, స్వర్గం కోరేవారు, మోక్షం కోరే కొద్దిమంది తమ మార్గాలను అనుసరిస్తారని చెబుతాడు.","ta":"பீஷ்மர் நிறுத்தியதும் தர்மம், பொருள், இன்பம் இவற்றில் எது பெரியது என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்க, அவை ஒன்றை ஒன்று சார்ந்தவை ஆனால் விடுதலையே எல்லாவற்றினும் மேல் என்று பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். செல்வம், சொர்க்கம், விடுதலை நாடுவோர் ஒவ்வொருவரும் தம் வழியைப் பின்பற்றுவர் என்கிறார்.","ml":"ഭീഷ്മർ നിർത്തിയശേഷം, ധർമ്മം, അർത്ഥം, കാമം എന്നിവയിൽ ഏതാണ് വലുതെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; ഇവ പരസ്പരം ആശ്രയിച്ചു നിൽക്കുന്നുവെങ്കിലും മോക്ഷമാണ് എല്ലാറ്റിനും മീതെയെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. ധനം ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നവരും സ്വർഗ്ഗം ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നവരും, ചുരുക്കം ചിലർ മോക്ഷം ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്നവരും തങ്ങളുടെ വഴി പിന്തുടരുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.161; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"आपद्धर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Apaddharma Parva (Duties in distress)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इत्युक्तवति भीष्मे तु तूष्णींभूते युधिष्ठिरः ।\nपप्रच्छावसरं गत्वा भ्रातॄन्विदुरपञ्चमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma had spoken thus and fallen silent, Yudhishthira found a moment and questioned his brothers, with Vidura as the fifth."}},{"n":2,"text":"धर्मे चार्थे च कामे च लोकवृत्तिः समाहिता ।\nतेषां गरीयान्कतमो मध्यमः को लघुश्च कः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The life of the world rests on dharma, wealth and desire. Which of these is the greatest, which the middle, and which the least?"}},{"n":3,"text":"कस्मिंश्चात्मा नियन्तव्यस्त्रिवर्गविजयाय वै ।\nसंतुष्टा नैष्ठिकं वाक्यं यथावद्वक्तुमर्हथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"On which should one fix oneself to win over the three? Being content, you should tell me your settled view as it is."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततोऽर्थगतितत्त्वज्ञः प्रथमं प्रतिभानवान् ।\nजगाद विदुरो वाक्यं धर्मशास्त्रमनुस्मरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vidura, who knew the truth of wealth and its paths and was gifted with ready insight, spoke first, recalling the dharma teachings."}},{"n":5,"text":"बाहुश्रुत्यं तपस्त्यागः श्रद्धा यज्ञक्रिया क्षमा ।\nभावशुद्धिर्दया सत्यं संयमश्चात्मसंपदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wide learning, austerity, renunciation, faith, sacrificial acts, forbearance, purity of feeling, kindness, truth and self-restraint are a man's inner wealth."}},{"n":6,"text":"एतदेवाभिपद्यस्व मा ते भूच्चलितं मनः ।\nएतन्मूलौ हि धर्मार्थावेतदेकपदं हितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hold to this alone and let your mind not waver; for dharma and wealth have this as their root, and this one thing is the good."}},{"n":7,"text":"धर्मेणैवर्षयस्तीर्णा धर्मे लोकाः प्रतिष्ठिताः ।\nधर्मेण देवा दिविगा धर्मे चार्थः समाहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By dharma the seers crossed over; the worlds are founded on dharma; by dharma the gods dwell in heaven, and wealth is grounded in dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"धर्मो राजन्गुणश्रेष्ठो मध्यमो ह्यर्थ उच्यते ।\nकामो यवीयानिति च प्रवदन्ति मनीषिणः ।\nतस्माद्धर्मप्रधानेन भवितव्यं यतात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, dharma is the best of qualities, wealth is called the middle, and desire the least, say the wise. Therefore one should put dharma first and keep himself controlled."}},{"n":9,"text":"समाप्तवचने तस्मिन्नर्थशास्त्रविशारदः ।\nपार्थो वाक्यार्थतत्त्वज्ञो जगौ वाक्यमतन्द्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had finished speaking, Arjuna, skilled in the science of wealth and knowing the truth of what was said, spoke tirelessly."}},{"n":10,"text":"कर्मभूमिरियं राजन्निह वार्त्ता प्रशस्यते ।\nकृषिवाणिज्यगोरक्ष्यं शिल्पानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, this is the world of action; here livelihood is praised: farming, trade, cattle-keeping and many kinds of crafts."}},{"n":11,"text":"अर्थ इत्येव सर्वेषां कर्मणामव्यतिक्रमः ।\nन ऋतेऽर्थेन वर्तेते धर्मकामाविति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All actions are held within wealth without exception; the scripture says dharma and desire do not go on without wealth."}},{"n":12,"text":"विजयी ह्यर्थवान्धर्ममाराधयितुमुत्तमम् ।\nकामं च चरितुं शक्तो दुष्प्रापमकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A conqueror with wealth can worship the highest dharma and enjoy desire, which are hard to gain for those with untrained selves."}},{"n":13,"text":"अर्थस्यावयवावेतौ धर्मकामाविति श्रुतिः ।\nअर्थसिद्ध्या हि निर्वृत्तावुभावेतौ भविष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma and desire are the two parts of wealth, says the tradition; when wealth is accomplished both will be fulfilled."}},{"n":14,"text":"उद्भूतार्थं हि पुरुषं विशिष्टतरयोनयः ।\nब्रह्माणमिव भूतानि सततं पर्युपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even people of higher birth always wait on a man of great wealth, as beings wait on Brahma."}},{"n":15,"text":"जटाजिनधरा दान्ताः पङ्कदिग्धा जितेन्द्रियाः ।\nमुण्डा निस्तन्तवश्चापि वसन्त्यर्थार्थिनः पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some wear matted hair and deerskins, are self-controlled, smeared with mud, masters of their senses, shaven and without a thread, and live apart seeking wealth."}},{"n":16,"text":"काषायवसनाश्चान्ये श्मश्रुला ह्रीसुसंवृताः ।\nविद्वांसश्चैव शान्ताश्च मुक्ताः सर्वपरिग्रहैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others wear ochre robes, are bearded and modest, learned and tranquil, free of all possessions."}},{"n":17,"text":"अर्थार्थिनः सन्ति केचिदपरे स्वर्गकाङ्क्षिणः ।\nकुलप्रत्यागमाश्चैके स्वं स्वं मार्गमनुष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some seek wealth, others long for heaven, and some follow family traditions, each treading his own path."}},{"n":18,"text":"आस्तिका नास्तिकाश्चैव नियताः संयमे परे ।\nअप्रज्ञानं तमोभूतं प्रज्ञानं तु प्रकाशता ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are believers and unbelievers, and others firm in restraint; lack of knowledge is darkness, and knowledge is light."}},{"n":19,"text":"भृत्यान्भोगैर्द्विषो दण्डैर्यो योजयति सोऽर्थवान् ।\nएतन्मतिमतां श्रेष्ठ मतं मम यथातथम् ।\nअनयोस्तु निबोध त्वं वचनं वाक्यकण्ठयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who rewards servants with enjoyments and enemies with punishment is a man of wealth. This, best of the wise, is my view as it is. Now hear the words of these two, who speak so well."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो धर्मार्थकुशलौ माद्रीपुत्रावनन्तरम् ।\nनकुलः सहदेवश्च वाक्यं जगदतुः परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sons of Madri, skilled in dharma and wealth, Nakula and Sahadeva, spoke next with excellent words."}},{"n":21,"text":"आसीनश्च शयानश्च विचरन्नपि च स्थितः ।\nअर्थयोगं दृढं कुर्याद्योगैरुच्चावचैरपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sitting, lying, walking or standing, one should make his hold on wealth firm, by all kinds of means."}},{"n":22,"text":"अस्मिंस्तु वै सुसंवृत्ते दुर्लभे परमप्रिये ।\nइह कामानवाप्नोति प्रत्यक्षं नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When this hard-to-get and dearest thing is well secured, one gains one's desires right here, in plain sight; there is no doubt."}},{"n":23,"text":"योऽर्थो धर्मेण संयुक्तो धर्मो यश्चार्थसंयुतः ।\nमध्विवामृतसंयुक्तं तस्मादेतौ मताविह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth joined with dharma and dharma joined with wealth are like honey mixed with nectar; so both are valued here."}},{"n":24,"text":"अनर्थस्य न कामोऽस्ति तथार्थोऽधर्मिणः कुतः ।\nतस्मादुद्विजते लोको धर्मार्थाद्यो बहिष्कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One without wealth has no desire, nor does the wealth of an unrighteous man come easily; so the world shrinks from a man shut out of dharma and wealth."}},{"n":25,"text":"तस्माद्धर्मप्रधानेन साध्योऽर्थः संयतात्मना ।\nविश्वस्तेषु च भूतेषु कल्पते सर्व एव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So wealth should be earned by one who puts dharma first and is self-controlled; for when beings trust him, everything becomes possible."}},{"n":26,"text":"धर्मं समाचरेत्पूर्वं तथार्थं धर्मसंयुतम् ।\nततः कामं चरेत्पश्चात्सिद्धार्थस्य हि तत्फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should practise dharma first, then wealth joined with dharma, and afterward desire; for that is the fruit for one whose purpose is achieved."}},{"n":27,"text":"विरेमतुस्तु तद्वाक्यमुक्त्वा तावश्विनोः सुतौ ।\nभीमसेनस्तदा वाक्यमिदं वक्तुं प्रचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the two sons of the Ashvins stopped. Then Bhimasena began to speak these words."}},{"n":28,"text":"नाकामः कामयत्यर्थं नाकामो धर्ममिच्छति ।\nनाकामः कामयानोऽस्ति तस्मात्कामो विशिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One without desire does not seek wealth, one without desire does not want dharma, and none exists who is not desiring; so desire is greater."}},{"n":29,"text":"कामेन युक्ता ऋषयस्तपस्येव समाहिताः ।\nपलाशफलमूलाशा वायुभक्षाः सुसंयताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seers are moved by desire, absorbed in austerity, living on palasha fruits and roots or on air, very restrained."}},{"n":30,"text":"वेदोपवादेष्वपरे युक्ताः स्वाध्यायपारगाः ।\nश्राद्धयज्ञक्रियायां च तथा दानप्रतिग्रहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Others are engaged in disputes over the Vedas, masters of their recitation, and in ancestral offerings, sacrifices, giving and receiving gifts."}},{"n":31,"text":"वणिजः कर्षका गोपाः कारवः शिल्पिनस्तथा ।\nदैवकर्मकृतश्चैव युक्ताः कामेन कर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Merchants, farmers, herdsmen, craftsmen and artisans, and those who do rites for the gods are all engaged in their work by desire."}},{"n":32,"text":"समुद्रं चाविशन्त्यन्ये नराः कामेन संयुताः ।\nकामो हि विविधाकारः सर्वं कामेन संततम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other men, moved by desire, even enter the ocean. Desire has many forms, and everything is always driven by desire."}},{"n":33,"text":"नास्ति नासीन्नाभविष्यद्भूतं कामात्मकात्परम् ।\nएतत्सारं महाराज धर्मार्थावत्र संश्रितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is not, was not and will not be a being beyond one made of desire. This is the essence, great king; dharma and wealth rest upon it."}},{"n":34,"text":"नवनीतं यथा दध्नस्तथा कामोऽर्थधर्मतः ।\nश्रेयस्तैलं च पिण्याकाद्घृतं श्रेय उदश्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As butter is to curds, so desire is to wealth and dharma; oil is better than the cake, ghee better than the buttermilk,"}},{"n":35,"text":"श्रेयः पुष्पफलं काष्ठात्कामो धर्मार्थयोर्वरः ।\nपुष्पतो मध्विव रसः कामात्संजायते सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"flower and fruit better than the wood; desire is better than dharma and wealth. As honey's sweetness comes from the flower, pleasure is born of desire."}},{"n":36,"text":"सुचारुवेषाभिरलंकृताभि-\nर्मदोत्कटाभिः प्रियवादिनीभिः ।\nरमस्व योषाभिरुपेत्य कामं\nकामो हि राजंस्तरसाभिपाती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go and enjoy your desire with women beautifully dressed, bold with passion and sweet in speech; for desire, king, comes swiftly."}},{"n":37,"text":"बुद्धिर्ममैषा परिषत्स्थितस्य\nमा भूद्विचारस्तव धर्मपुत्र ।\nस्यात्संहितं सद्भिरफल्गुसारं\nसमेत्य वाक्यं परमानृशंस्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is my view, as I sit in this assembly. Let there be no doubt in you, son of Dharma; this would be a speech that the good would approve, not empty but substantial, and wholly kind."}},{"n":38,"text":"धर्मार्थकामाः सममेव सेव्या\nयस्त्वेकसेवी स नरो जघन्यः ।\nद्वयोस्तु दक्षं प्रवदन्ति मध्यं\nस उत्तमो यो निरतस्त्रिवर्गे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma, wealth and desire should be served equally; the man who serves only one is the lowest. The one who serves two is called the middle, and the best is he who is devoted to all three."}},{"n":39,"text":"प्राज्ञः सुहृच्चन्दनसारलिप्तो\nविचित्रमाल्याभरणैरुपेतः ।\nततो वचः संग्रहविग्रहेण\nप्रोक्त्वा यवीयान्विरराम भीमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wise Bhimasena, the youngest of the speakers, smeared with sandal paste for his friend and adorned with varied garlands and ornaments, then ended, having spoken briefly."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तादथ धर्मराजो\nवाक्यानि तेषामनुचिन्त्य सम्यक् ।\nउवाच वाचावितथं स्मयन्वै\nबहुश्रुतो धर्मभृतां वरिष्ठः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after a moment, the king of dharma, well-learned and best of those upholding dharma, thoughtfully weighed their words and spoke, smiling, with truthful speech."}},{"n":41,"text":"निःसंशयं निश्चितधर्मशास्त्राः\nसर्वे भवन्तो विदितप्रमाणाः ।\nविज्ञातुकामस्य ममेह वाक्य-\nमुक्तं यद्वै नैष्ठिकं तच्छ्रुतं मे ।\nइह त्ववश्यं गदतो ममापि\nवाक्यं निबोधध्वमनन्यभावाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No doubt all of you are settled in the dharma texts and know the standards. As I wished to understand, I have heard the final conclusion you each gave. Now I too must speak; listen to my words with undivided minds."}},{"n":42,"text":"यो वै न पापे निरतो न पुण्ये\nनार्थे न धर्मे मनुजो न कामे ।\nविमुक्तदोषः समलोष्टकाञ्चनः\nस मुच्यते दुःखसुखार्थसिद्धेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who delights neither in sin nor in merit, neither in wealth, nor in dharma, nor in desire, free of faults and viewing a clod and gold alike, is freed from the results of pain and pleasure."}},{"n":43,"text":"भूतानि जातीमरणान्वितानि\nजराविकारैश्च समन्वितानि ।\nभूयश्च तैस्तैः प्रतिबोधितानि\nमोक्षं प्रशंसन्ति न तं च विद्मः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beings are bound up with birth and death, and with the changes of old age; being awakened again and again by these, they praise liberation, but we do not know it."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्नेहे नबद्धस्य न सन्ति तानी-\nत्येवं स्वयंभूर्भगवानुवाच ।\nबुधाश्च निर्वाणपरा वदन्ति\nतस्मान्न कुर्यात्प्रियमप्रियं च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The divine Self-Born said that these do not exist for one not bound by affection. The wise who are devoted to extinction say so; therefore one should do nothing for what is pleasing or displeasing."}},{"n":45,"text":"एतत्प्रधानं न तु कामकारो\nयथा नियुक्तोऽस्मि तथा चरामि ।\nभूतानि सर्वाणि विधिर्नियुङ्क्ते\nविधिर्बलीयानिति वित्त सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is what matters, not acting at will. I act as I am directed; fate sets all beings to their tasks. Know all of you that fate is stronger."}},{"n":46,"text":"न कर्मणाप्नोत्यनवाप्यमर्थं\nयद्भावि सर्वं भवतीति वित्त ।\nत्रिवर्गहीनोऽपि हि विन्दतेऽर्थं\nतस्मादिदं लोकहिताय गुह्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One does not gain by action what cannot be had; know that whatever is to be, will be. One lacking the three aims may still gain wealth; so this is a secret for the good of the world."}},{"n":47,"text":"ततस्तदग्र्यं वचनं मनोनुगं\nसमस्तमाज्ञाय ततोऽतिहेतुमत् ।\nतदा प्रणेदुश्च जहर्षिरे च ते\nकुरुप्रवीराय च चक्रुरञ्जलीन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having understood that supreme speech, so agreeable and so full of reason, they roared and rejoiced, and folded their hands to the best of the Kurus."}},{"n":48,"text":"सुचारुवर्णाक्षरशब्दभूषितां\nमनोनुगां निर्धुतवाक्यकण्टकाम् ।\nनिशम्य तां पार्थिव पार्थभाषितां\nगिरं नरेन्द्राः प्रशशंसुरेव ते ।\nपुनश्च पप्रच्छ सरिद्वरासुतं\nततः परं धर्ममहीनसत्त्वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those words spoken by the son of Pritha, graceful in colour, letter and sound, pleasing to the mind and free of thorny speech, the kings praised them. Then he of undiminished spirit again questioned the son of the great river."}}]}]}